    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ad57021_49dcf172",
        "filename": "util/ec_panicinfo.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-08T00:03:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e That is, ectool is agnostic about the board (but aware of ARCH\u003dx64/arm) because ectool is built with BOARD\u003dhost.\n\nNot always. The utils are also built for the boards, which is where this was failing. For example: `make BOARD\u003dnocturne`.\n\n\u003e Also, enum panic_arch is defined in panic.h. Is it exported (like ec_commands.h)?\n\nI don\u0027t think so. It\u0027s just getting included through `ec_panicinfo.h`, which includes `panic.h`.",
      "parentUuid": "e22be05e_1b8806be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 210,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "10943e00138a364ad4dfd1745423e545285227bb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
